{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:41:12Z","created_by_operation":"op_3f6b3eeb40ab4d939f1dafcdfcc84c89","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_0b514cbb947b741ec1c797a425cf3505288d34db966a872ed76c58c3151ad3ae","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=specifications","setting":"solo-agent/solo@9d58e66769ed snapshot e6a9f00ed7f2beb8","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_871925af40129c5d0b2fe99ad8d311d435ac83b192a566d566cdd0824515e8ea"],"source_ids":["src_de05b9dbede4509687b6e48c6e693a78"],"text":"Solo is described as an open-source, local-first workspace for humans and AI coding agents, coordinating multiple agents through channels, threaded conversations, task boards, and channel-scoped teams.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:41:12Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3f6b3eeb40ab4d939f1dafcdfcc84c89"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:41:12Z","created_by_operation":"op_3f6b3eeb40ab4d939f1dafcdfcc84c89","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_0e957804a6fde39af42bbf63f7dc13f496b87342bfb7d049e61f83cdced2bcb8","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=skills-patterns","setting":"solo-agent/solo@9d58e66769ed snapshot e6a9f00ed7f2beb8","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_df8ec7096c42af0f99caa23bdb1f03d8fbe8b0bfd7b92fdf69766479e4e4a04a"],"source_ids":["src_de05b9dbede4509687b6e48c6e693a78"],"text":"Agent team templates let users choose an official workflow or describe a goal to Lucy, preview roles and working relationships, and create agents scoped to one channel with post-creation tuning.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:41:12Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3f6b3eeb40ab4d939f1dafcdfcc84c89"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:41:12Z","created_by_operation":"op_3f6b3eeb40ab4d939f1dafcdfcc84c89","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_15cf1d0db2c4cccc6a46acb0b76d7eea0f05ff41c1f47ce920fe75484f6fe990","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"solo-agent/solo@9d58e66769ed snapshot e6a9f00ed7f2beb8","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_4992547457393703c9460caa9d0512744636505a728b08b18ebfe619963a57da","slc_60492cd464a7e15b7db814345059378fa2263edba953b064c82288ad7323ec84"],"source_ids":["src_de05b9dbede4509687b6e48c6e693a78"],"text":"Solo runs three local layers: a Go API server on :8080 with WebSocket hub, auth, and PostgreSQL persistence; a daemon on :8081 that registers the machine and manages agent subprocesses; and the installed agent CLI driven over stdin/stdout.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:41:12Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3f6b3eeb40ab4d939f1dafcdfcc84c89"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:41:12Z","created_by_operation":"op_3f6b3eeb40ab4d939f1dafcdfcc84c89","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_1d9f9ac6866d63bc8298d126deccc1fecaa2ce7c96b9b9f2073635243c8be4b6","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"solo-agent/solo@9d58e66769ed snapshot e6a9f00ed7f2beb8","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0839ac56c7b7577d55702a55cd701ea5bef94582c8820f58cab77a2950330108","slc_2831f454421340fd397332adda41b70a512f0162ce0efdf263a7ccc7f08ffd82"],"source_ids":["src_de05b9dbede4509687b6e48c6e693a78"],"text":"Agent backends are auto-detected from PATH at daemon startup: Claude Code via stream-json, Codex CLI via JSON-RPC, and OpenCode, Hermes, and OpenClaw via ACP.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:41:12Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3f6b3eeb40ab4d939f1dafcdfcc84c89"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:41:12Z","created_by_operation":"op_3f6b3eeb40ab4d939f1dafcdfcc84c89","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_2c98d456627272e3e128f2df6d724ee230d45bbae284c9036c1f36e71276d13d","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=workflows","setting":"solo-agent/solo@9d58e66769ed snapshot e6a9f00ed7f2beb8","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_5e1cb4ea949767adb78c3bfc2894ddb4d648385541a8b5523875f06d9646cb2c","slc_d4a476a189f3f6a20c5cca2361cc0e14a689ee256f0077cd767d80cbb3edafa8"],"source_ids":["src_2f5dfa42b3005ce0b474c44c84ed9f6c"],"text":"Repository development practice: the changelog reports real end-to-end test coverage for workspaces, multi-daemon execution, automations, token accounting, remote uploads, governance, wake coalescing, and runtime capability detection.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:41:12Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3f6b3eeb40ab4d939f1dafcdfcc84c89"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:41:12Z","created_by_operation":"op_3f6b3eeb40ab4d939f1dafcdfcc84c89","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_362ac9079c62f9f7df5383f7988b6472e0f438c10aa6f0bfa2870bb41dce21ff","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"solo-agent/solo@9d58e66769ed snapshot e6a9f00ed7f2beb8","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_8c0d5175655e1e08853b0749eda53c60818f874a37731c5523044e6cd41ecfae","slc_cb0319c2c81922e307ec1226d828ccbb99253a2d15b89198b809de7523e7eeff"],"source_ids":["src_de05b9dbede4509687b6e48c6e693a78"],"text":"Agents keep agent-specific MEMORY.md context that is loaded into future sessions, and the comparison table says agents retain long-term memory, their own environment, and a fixed workspace.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:41:12Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3f6b3eeb40ab4d939f1dafcdfcc84c89"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:41:12Z","created_by_operation":"op_3f6b3eeb40ab4d939f1dafcdfcc84c89","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_3fb7485119e0352cb1f6ee6406d436717ccabe1e2f97fb79f4b3baefd729929e","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"solo-agent/solo@9d58e66769ed snapshot e6a9f00ed7f2beb8","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_fceb92b33334701965a4cf94ec3205bc189b7df439b6037bef8befc2e2675d16"],"source_ids":["src_2f5dfa42b3005ce0b474c44c84ed9f6c"],"text":"Solo supports remote deployment: the web app, API, PostgreSQL, attachments, and artifacts can run on a remote server while agent runtimes and credentials stay local, with one-time pairing tokens and a `solo` CLI for daemon management.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:41:12Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3f6b3eeb40ab4d939f1dafcdfcc84c89"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:41:12Z","created_by_operation":"op_3f6b3eeb40ab4d939f1dafcdfcc84c89","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_529591f0951196d4ec30731b943fa0fbfc9915c5fbd0fcaba7ecc87e32c497a3","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"solo-agent/solo@9d58e66769ed snapshot e6a9f00ed7f2beb8","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_d3b0f738374f926eb3ed300938a78c4cfb76512efe6f619f28999742ac8808c9"],"source_ids":["src_de05b9dbede4509687b6e48c6e693a78"],"text":"The runtime topology is Browser (Next.js :3000) to Server (Go :8080) over WebSocket, Server to Daemon over HTTP/SSE, and Daemon to Agent CLI over stdin/stdout.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:41:12Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3f6b3eeb40ab4d939f1dafcdfcc84c89"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:41:12Z","created_by_operation":"op_3f6b3eeb40ab4d939f1dafcdfcc84c89","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_5b760d4977d82ca2ac227b16909fbb9e1341fb7b80980924261609bed3f5b9f1","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=workflows","setting":"solo-agent/solo@9d58e66769ed snapshot e6a9f00ed7f2beb8","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0d6beedd65b6798171b74d6d66ab5e9d7b92869de4a5064c0f1633234f20c479"],"source_ids":["src_109c906d1405539e941e767ff6c01186"],"text":"Repository development practice: agents may restart the frontend, API server, and daemon only via `make rebuild` from the repo root, and must never use launchctl, direct binaries, go run, npm run dev, nohup, or custom background commands.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:41:12Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3f6b3eeb40ab4d939f1dafcdfcc84c89"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:41:12Z","created_by_operation":"op_3f6b3eeb40ab4d939f1dafcdfcc84c89","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_670bee5f77ec370c6c4236289435da15ba5154dedf31b53a8195ad5232edaf3c","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"solo-agent/solo@9d58e66769ed snapshot e6a9f00ed7f2beb8","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_8209d22a736fa73c2a0ab794aa8d4b97c2366761f59782735902061b20cf6c6e"],"source_ids":["src_de05b9dbede4509687b6e48c6e693a78"],"text":"Solo is intentionally a workspace rather than a company simulator, where agents can be mentioned, assigned, reviewed, remembered, and trusted with visible work.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:41:12Z","updated_by_operation":"op_3f6b3eeb40ab4d939f1dafcdfcc84c89"}
